//! Named-view help (V12).

pub(super) const HELP: &str = "Model views (V12): named views with their own view plane and display properties, kept in a session JSON file beside the model; the store is never written. list-views --file FILE returns the folders and every view. save-view --file FILE [--name NAME] creates a view from exactly one plane: an orbit --yaw RAD --pitch RAD [--target X,Y,Z]; a coordinate plane --parallel xy|xz|yz [--offset MM]; an explicit frame --plane OX,OY,OZ,XX,XY,XZ,YX,YY,YZ; --two-points A;B (vertical, or across the input plane given by --work-plane); --three-points A;B;C; or, reading the model through --store ROOT: --grid SELECTOR --axis LABEL (one axis) or --grid SELECTOR [--u-axes none|first|last|all] [--v-axes ...] [--u-prefix TEXT] [--v-prefix TEXT] (one view per axis, named prefix and label), --level NAME|ID or --levels first|last|all, --element ID or --assembly ID with --side front|back|top|bottom|end|3d|four (four creates front, top, end and 3d), and --ray-origin X,Y,Z --ray-direction X,Y,Z [--edge A;B] (the first face hit). Without --name a single view is named View N (the lowest free number) and a batch by its labels alone. Batches add all views or none and suffix repeated names. Display properties, for save-view and update-view: --projection, --span MM (visible height), --depth none|ABOVE,BELOW (distance shown towards the viewer and behind the plane), --rotation Z_DEG,X_DEG (turns the camera, not the plane), --render-mode, --grids, --hidden-kinds none|KIND,..., --work-area none|six numbers, --color default|R,G,B (0..1), --opacity 0..1, --folder PATH, --favorite, --default true|false (the one default view of the model: setting it moves the mark, and the default view cannot be removed or unmarked), --copy-from VIEW. update-view --file FILE --view ID|NAME [--name NEW] changes one view, its plane through any single-view option. remove-view and apply-view take --view ID|NAME; apply-view returns the view, its camera frame and its clip planes, without touching any store. View filters, filter overrides and view presets live in the same file. list-view-filters --file FILE returns the filters and presets. save-view-filter --file FILE --name NAME [--rename-from OLD] [--match all|any] [--conditions none|ROW;...] adds or changes a filter; a ROW is `field op value` with field type, name, class or attribute:NAME and op eq, ne, lt, le, gt, ge, contains or starts-with, for example `type eq beam;class ge 2`; a rename follows into every view and preset. remove-view-filter --file FILE --name NAME removes it and every override that names it. save-view and update-view take --overrides none|SPEC;... (a SPEC is `filter|show or hide|R,G,B or -|transparency`, the first matching override decides how an element is drawn) and --preset NAME (fills the display properties from a preset, keeping no link). save-view-preset --file FILE --name NAME --from-view VIEW saves a view's display properties as a preset; remove-view-preset --file FILE --name NAME removes one.";
